strlen^#^
SUBTOPIC-efun^#^
EFUN strlen()

SYNOPSIS
     int strlen(string str);

DESCRIPTION
     strlen() returns the number  of  characters  in  the  string
     `str'.

EXAMPLE

string last_letter(string str) {
  if(!str || str == "") return "";
  return str[(strlen(str)-1)..(strlen(str)-1)];
}

SEE ALSO
     sizeof(), extract(), []^#^
